        "code": "IVR-CRS-MWA84BFT",
        "title": "VLSI Design & Verification Using Verilog HDL",
        "domain": "VLSI Design & Verification Using Verilog HDL",
        "description": "This internship program focuses on the software-oriented aspects of VLSI design, including Verilog HDL programming, RTL design, digital circuit simulation, and functional verification. Students will gain practical experience using industry-relevant EDA tools, writing and debugging HDL code, designing digital systems, and verifying hardware functionality through software-based simulation and project development.",
        "department": "ECE",
        "durationWeeks": 8,
        "level": "Intermediate",
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "syllabus": "Module 1: Introduction to VLSI Design and EDA Tools\n\nModule 2: Digital Electronics and Logic Design\n\nModule 3: Verilog HDL Programming Fundamentals\n\nModule 4: RTL Design and Coding Techniques\n\nModule 5: Digital Circuit Simulation Using EDA Tools\n\nModule 6: Functional Verification and Testbench Development\n\nModule 7: FPGA Design and Implementation Basics\n\nModule 8: Final Project – Design, Simulation and Verification of a Digital System",
